  "description": "Whether a file a local .NET host is about to run comes from the publisher it expects: on Windows a valid Authenticode signature checked the way Windows checks it (WinVerifyTrust, offline) with the verified signer's certificate subject matched against the publishers the caller names; on macOS a valid code signature checked by the system (codesign) from an expected Developer ID team, optionally notarized — so a renewed certificate keeps passing and a validly signed file from anyone else does not.",
